  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $7$ is a composite number and odd. This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a composite number}}_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd} }_B,\n\\]\nthat is, $A \\land B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $2+6 \\geq 10.$ This corresponds to $C.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\\[\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a composite number} \\textbf{ and } \\textrm{odd} }_{A \\, \\land \\, B}, \\quad \n\\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \n\\underbrace{2+6 \\geq 10 }_C \n\\]\nthat is, $(A \\land B) \\lor C.$",
