  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-177454\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".</p>\n<p>Note that this sentence consists of two parts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Part 1:</strong> $7$ is a composite number and odd. This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a composite number}}_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd} }_B,\n\\]\nthat is, $A \\land B.$ </p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Part 2:</strong> $2+6 \\geq 10.$ This corresponds to $C.$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So, we can express the sentence as\n\\[\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a composite number} \\textbf{ and } \\textrm{odd} }_{A \\, \\land \\, B}, \\quad \n\\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \n\\underbrace{2+6 \\geq 10 }_C \n\\]\nthat is, $(A \\land B) \\lor C.$</p>\n</div>",
